The main thing I learned from this lecture is that automation can save a lot of time when the same task has to be done over and over.

I liked that n8n does not require a lot of normal programming. You can connect different steps together and make a workflow without writing everything from scratch.

The human-in-the-loop part also made sense to me. AI can help make a decision or create a response, but a person can still check it before anything happens. I think that makes automation safer and more useful.

